I've written the Day 232 assessment to session_plan/assessment.md and committed it as 40875c69. The folder is gitignored, so I used git add -f, which is how the 18:28 assessment got committed too.

The main finding is that the dependency bump at HEAD (73e5c3ac, yoagent 0.25.7 → 0.25.8) changed things my code and docs still describe the old way:

• Background jobs in `bash` get killed. Since the #1049 fix, my bash tool stops reading a command's output 2 seconds after it ends. I tested it live with yoyo -p: a background job that prints something after that point dies on the write. Its marker file never appeared, while the same job without the print wrote its file. yoagent 0.25.8's own bash handles this case by keeping on reading and throwing the output away, so the job survives. That's a ready-made reference for the fix.
• Stale claims.
  • src/non_regular_read.rs:3 says yoagent's read_file hangs on pipes, which 0.25.8 fixed.
  • ARCHITECTURE.md:1530 describes a version gap that closed long ago.
  • The 08:32 journal calls two upstream reports #1050 and #1051, but those numbers don't exist in this repo. The real ones are yoagent#341 and #342, both closed by this release.
• Yuanhao spelled out the next work on #1037 at 22:30Z. Use yoagent's new Sonnet and Haiku 5.5 settings and delete my hand-built copies. Add gpt-6.1-sol and make it the OpenAI default. Add entries for the new Gemini, Grok, Mistral and GLM models. He also flagged that the tests in model_limits_note.rs that assume gpt-6.1-sol has no preset will go stale; they should point at a still-unknown model rather than be deleted.

What I re-checked on the current binary:
• #982 (exit-code bugs): doctor, help, update and init still accept a stray word and exit 0, and init zzz writes YOYO.md. config show on an unreadable or FIFO .yoyo.toml prints the error but exits 0.
• #1047 (FIFO reads): two reads in src/config_paths.rs (lines 299 and 326) still don't check what kind of file they're opening. I posted these rows on #1047 at the bump's commit.
• File-size limits are tight:
  • config.rs: 11 lines left.
  • tools.rs: about 17 lines left.
  • commands_risk_unhittable.rs: 14 lines left, and it isn't on the oversize list.

  New tests should go in sibling *_tests.rs files.

The last ten sessions were all 2/2, with no CI failures or reverts in 14 days. I didn't rerun the full test suite; the harness had already verified this commit.

On research: Claude Code v2.1.302 fixed the same pipe-named-as-an-image read bug as #1047. I saved a short note on that and on the background-job difference to yopedia.

The suggested order for the planner:
1. A first #1037 slice: swap in yoagent's 5.5 presets and add the gpt-6.1-sol default. It should remove more lines than it adds.
2. Match yoagent's background-job handling in bash without losing the quick exit from #1049.
3. Close out the #1047 rows and stale comments, and make config show fail when it can't read the file (#982).

